name: interview-me
description: "Interviews the user one question at a time to uncover who, why, success, and constraints. Use when a request is underspecified or the user says interview me."
---

# Interview Me

Extract what the user wants before any plan or code. One question at a time, until about 95% confidence.

## Process

1. Hypothesize with a defensible confidence number.
2. Ask one question, with a guess:
   ```
   Q: <one focused question>
   GUESS: <your hypothesis and why>
   ```
   Never batch questions.
3. Reflect want vs should-want.
4. Stop near 95%. Then hand off to `spec-driven-development`.

## Verification

You can state the user, the job to be done, the success measure, and the confirmed constraint.
